-- title:
--   Lower bound [F:K(x)] ≤ deg of the pole divisor
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra satisfying `IsCurveOver K F`, i.e. $F/K$ has principal divisors (every nonzero $f \in F$ is the divisor-valued datum of its orders $\operatorname{ord}_v f$ at all places, with total degree $0$), every place has residue field finite over $K$, and $\Omega[F/K]$ is free of rank $1$ over $F$; here a place is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring, and $\operatorname{ord}_v$ is minus the logarithm of the associated $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation. Assume further that $\mathcal L(0) = \{f \in F : v(f) \le 1 \text{ for all } v\}$ is finite-dimensional over $K$. Let $x \in F$ be transcendental over $K$, assume $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(x)$ generated by $x$, and let $D$ be a (finitely supported) divisor with $D(v) = \max(0, -\operatorname{ord}_v x)$ at every place $v$. Then $[F : K(x)] \le \deg D$, where $\deg D = \sum_v D(v) \cdot \deg v$, as an inequality of integers.
--
--   This is one half of the classical identity $\deg(x)_\infty = [F:K(x)]$ for a one-variable function field, the direction obtained by counting dimensions of Riemann–Roch spaces; no separability of $F/K(x)$ is required. It is cited in the proof of the corresponding equality [`AlgebraicCurve.Divisor.degree_eq_finrank_adjoin_of_eq_max_neg_ord`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Divisor.degree_eq_finrank_adjoin_of_eq_max_neg_ord).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Divisor_finrank_adjoin_le_degree_of_eq_max_neg_ord.lean

import Mathlib
